Subject: One MMIO decoder for every device, covering what any compiler emits

The NV2A, APU and OHCI registers are emulated by trapping the access and decoding the host instruction
that made it. There were three decoders, each covering the MOV forms MSVC emitted for the volatile
guest accesses. clang folds such a load into the instruction that uses it, so a clang build stopped at
its first OHCI poll on `and edx,[rcx+rax]`. All three devices now share platform/mmio_decode.h, which
decodes by encoding: MOV, MOVZX, MOVSX and MOVSXD, the ALU group (add, or, adc, sbb, and, sub, xor,
cmp) in both directions and with immediates, TEST, IMUL, BT, and the SSE scalar moves, with the
high-byte registers and the flags set as the CPU sets them. The length of a SIB operand without a base
was one disp32 short in all three. Anything else is still refused, so the device reports it.

